\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 1. Research\

\f1\b0 \

\fs24 A few platforms already cover pieces of the parking problem, but none of them put live availability, reservations, in-app navigation, and operator analytics into one system. Here's what I found when I looked at what's already out there.\
\
\uc0\u9679  SpotHero: A web and mobile marketplace for pre-booking parking at garages and lots. Checkout is smooth, but it only covers partnered facilities and doesn't show live occupancy. Spots are sold from a fixed allotment, not tracked in real time.\
\
\uc0\u9679  ParkWhiz: Works a lot like SpotHero, but leans heavily on event and venue parking such as concerts and stadiums. Good if you're planning ahead, not much help for parking on the fly.\
\
\uc0\u9679  ParkMobile: A pay-by-phone app used by a lot of U.S. cities, mostly for on-street metered parking. Great city coverage, but weak when it comes to garage reservations, live availability maps, or anything for operators.\
\
\uc0\u9679  Passport Parking: Municipal parking and curb-management software sold to city governments. Strong on enforcement and compliance, but it's built for cities, not as an app drivers use directly.\
\
\uc0\u9679  Google Maps (parking difficulty indicator): Gives a general sense of whether parking will be \'93harder or easier than usual\'94 in some cities, but there's no reservation, no payment, and no actual space counts per facility.\
\
None of these solutions brings together live availability per facility, in-app reservation and payment, turn-by-turn navigation, and an operator dashboard for occupancy and analytics. Most tools pick a side: SpotHero, ParkWhiz, and ParkMobile serve drivers, while Passport serves cities and operators. The Smart Parking Platform is meant to serve both sides from the same system, and to do it with real-time data instead of pre-sold allotments.
\fs32 \
\

\f0\b 2. Vision and Scope\

\f1\b0 \

\f0\b\fs28 Project Background\

\f1\b0\fs24 \
We are $oftware \'a2orp. A software development studio. This project came about after parking facility operators and city transportation stakeholders flagged a recurring problem: drivers waste a lot of time hunting for open spaces, which adds to congestion and eats into people's day, while operators don't have good real-time tools to manage occupancy or pricing.
\fs32 \
\

\f0\b\fs28 Vision Statement\

\f1\b0\fs32 \

\fs24 For drivers who need to find and reserve parking quickly, and for operators who need to manage and understand their facilities, the Smart Parking Platform is a web and mobile system that offers real-time availability, in-app reservation and payment, and operator analytics. Existing tools only cover one side of that; this one covers both.\

\fs32 \

\f0\b\fs28 Scope\

\f1\b0\fs32 \

\fs24 Scope includes the driver-facing web and mobile experience (search, map, reserve, pay, get notified) along with an operator-facing admin dashboard (managing availability and pricing, viewing occupancy reports). Mapping and payments will be handled through third-party providers rather than built from scratch. Hardware or IoT sensors for physical occupancy detection are not part of this build; that data is assumed to come in as a feed. City-government enforcement tooling is also not included.\
