\f0\b\fs28 3.1 Introduction\

\f1\b0\fs24 \
Purpose: This document defines the requirements for the Smart Parking Platform, a web and mobile system that helps drivers find, reserve, and pay for parking in real time, and gives parking operators tools to manage availability, pricing, and occupancy.\
\
Scope: The platform covers a driver-facing web and mobile app (search, live availability map, reservations, payment, notifications) and an operator-facing admin dashboard (availability and pricing management, occupancy reporting). Hardware or IoT sensor development for physical occupancy detection is out of scope; that data is assumed to come in as a feed. City-government enforcement tooling is also out of scope.\
\

\f0\b\fs28 3.2 Overall Description\

\f1\b0\fs24 \
Users: Drivers and vehicle owners, parking facility operators, system administrators, and finance/billing personnel.\
\
System Environment: Web-based and mobile application (iOS and Android).\
\

\f0\b\fs28 3.3 Functional and Non-Functional Requirements\

\f1\b0\fs24 \

\f0\b Functional Requirements:\

\f1\b0 \
FR1: The system shall allow drivers to register and log in securely.\
\
FR2: The system shall allow drivers to search for parking near a destination.\
\
FR3: The system shall display real-time space availability on an interactive map.\
\
FR4: The system shall allow drivers to reserve a specific parking spot or space class.\
\
FR5: The system shall allow drivers to pay for a reservation digitally.\
\
FR6: The system shall generate a confirmation and receipt after payment.\
\
FR7: The system shall allow drivers to view, cancel, or modify reservations.\
\
FR8: The system shall provide navigation to a reserved spot through an integrated mapping service.\
\
FR9: The system shall send notifications for reservation status, low availability, and payment issues.\
\
FR10: The system shall allow parking operators to log into an admin dashboard.\
\
FR11: The system shall allow operators to update facility availability and pricing.\
\
FR12: The system shall provide operators with occupancy reporting and analytics.\
\
FR13: The system shall allow operators to manage facility listings.\
\
\

\f0\b\fs28 Non-Functional Requirements:\

\f1\b0\fs24 \
NFR1: The system shall support at least 1,000 concurrent users.\
\
NFR2: The map and availability data shall update within 5 seconds of a change.\
\
NFR3: The system shall provide 99.9% uptime.\
\
NFR4: Payment processing shall comply with PCI-DSS standards.\
\
\

\f0\b\fs32 3. Use Cases\

\f1\b0\fs24 \
UC-01\
Driver\
Register account\
A new driver creates an account using email or mobile number to access the platform.\
\
UC-02\
Driver\
Log in / authenticate\
A returning driver logs in securely to access reservations and account details.\
\
UC-03\
Driver\
Search for parking near destination\
Driver enters or selects a destination and the system returns nearby parking facilities.\
\
UC-04\
Driver\
View real-time availability on map\
Driver views an interactive map showing live open and occupied spot counts per facility.\
\
UC-05\
Driver\
Reserve a parking spot\
Driver selects a facility and time window and reserves a specific spot or space class.\
\
UC-06\
Driver\
Pay for reservation digitally\
Driver completes payment via card, digital wallet, or saved payment method.\
\
UC-07\
Driver\
Receive reservation confirmation and receipt\
System generates a digital confirmation and receipt after successful payment.\
\
UC-08\
Driver\
View reservation history\
Driver reviews past and upcoming reservations, including receipts.\
\
UC-09\
Driver\
Cancel or modify a reservation\
Driver cancels or changes an existing reservation within the allowed policy window.\
\
UC-10\
Driver\
Navigate to reserved spot\
System hands off to an integrated mapping and navigation service to route the driver to the facility.\
\
UC-11\
Driver\
Receive alerts and notifications\
Driver is notified of reservation expiration, low availability at a saved location, or payment issues.\
\
UC-12\
Parking Operator\
Log into admin dashboard\
An authorized operator logs into the facility management dashboard.\
\
UC-13\
Parking Operator\
Update facility availability and pricing\
Operator adjusts live space counts, pricing tiers, and blackout dates.\
\
UC-14\
Parking Operator\
View occupancy reporting and analytics\
Operator reviews utilization trends, peak hours, and revenue reports.\
\
UC-15\
Parking Operator\
Manage facility listings\
Operator adds, edits, or deactivates a parking facility profile on the platform.}